Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Ordinary play zoom implemented and locally qualified; publication pending.
Dependencies: Completed workstreams 25 and 31.

Purpose
-------
Expose the fullscreen-style zoom slider during ordinary handheld play without
requiring browser fullscreen or altering the native emulator.

Tasks
-----
[x] Add a themed accessible 50-100% play-only slider with percentage output.
[x] Scale the existing camera distance; retain the ordinary 100% framing.
[x] Keep play, inspection and fullscreen zoom independent.
[x] Retain the play percentage through Inspect/table returns and resize.
[x] Hide during transitions, table/Inspect and screen-only fullscreen.
[x] Check desktop/landscape/phone fit, native input/runtime and existing framing.
[x] Review actual desktop/320px captures and update affected documentation.
[ ] Publish through the normal complete gate and independently verify the live site.

Acceptance criteria
-------------------
100% preserves the existing fitted handheld; 50% pulls back without cropping
the LCD or changing core pixels, sound, speed, power or saves. The widget remains
outside the LCD, hardware targets, status and dock at the checked viewports.
Pointer/touch range input and keyboard Home/End/arrows update the displayed
percentage. Inspect zoom/reset and fullscreen zoom never overwrite play zoom.

Completion evidence
-------------------
HandheldScene retains an independent playZoom=.5..1 camera-distance divisor;
the existing inspection multiplier/reset and 100% fit remain unchanged.
Reframe/transition/resize reuse that same target calculation. The widget shares
fullscreen styling, sits bottom-right on wide screens and uses the hidden
header's top-left space on narrow/short screens, avoiding changes to framing
or dock position. The setting lasts for this page session, not across reloads.
Syntax/build/all11units pass. Three affected actual Edge cases pass in1.2m:
new original-Pixel-Lab zoom/lifecycle/input case19.4s, existing complete quick
actions/fullscreen case39.9s and physical branding/ordinary framing case11.9s.
Checked1440x1100,844x390,390x844,320x568; actual desktop/320px captures reviewed.
An initial fixture wrongly closed an already auto-closed drawer; corrected the
fixture, not the application. An intersection assertion also showed ordinary
DOM geometry remains in the viewport under native fullscreen; explicitly hide
the ordinary widget on fullscreenchange and verify that lifecycle directly.
No new private-ROM/audio replay, user aesthetic approval or deployment claimed.

